    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Fix Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file.\n\n**The Problem:**\nThe `gate` command in the frai CLI was using Commander.js's positional argument capture (`[args...]`), but Commander treats `--ci` as an option, not a positional argument. This meant the `--ci` flag never made it into the `args` array passed to the action handler, so it wasn't forwarded to the `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**The Solution:**\nModified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-755) to use `process.argv` directly instead of relying on Commander's parsed arguments. This ensures all arguments and flags that follow `gate` are correctly forwarded to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**The Change:**\n```typescript\n// Before: only passed positional args, missing --ci flag\nconst result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...(args ?? [])], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n\n// After: passes all raw arguments from process.argv\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.findIndex((arg) => arg === 'gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : [];\nconst result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...gateArgs], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n\u2705 Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`  \n\u2705 Tested the command and confirmed both files are now created:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\nThe workflow file is properly formatted and ready for CI/CD use.",
